  "id": "Compound::DB00422 - Gene::6532",
  "verbalization": "Methylphenidate and Dexmethylphenidate, both derivatives of methylphenidate, are known to bind to Slc6a4, a transporter protein involved in the reuptake of neurotransmitters. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, suggesting a general mechanism by which these compounds interact with Slc6a4. The evidence indicates that Methylphenidate and its metabolite Dexmethylphenidate, through a common pathway, exert effects that lead to the binding of Slc6a4. The presence of a lowest common ancestor (LCA) linking Methylphenidate and Dexmethylphenidate to the Cns Stimulant and Nitrogen Molecular Entity further supports a shared biological context. While the exact mechanism of Slc6a4 interaction remains somewhat indirect, the consistent binding across different effects implies a general role in neurotransmitter regulation, potentially influencing the function of Slc6a4 in neuronal activity. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role for Slc6a4 in the pharmacological actions of methylphenidate and its metabolites, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise functional relationship.",
